.TH "kome.conf" "5" "2026-10-25"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
kome.\&conf - kome'\&s settings, presets, palettes and styles
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
All of kome'\&s files are INI files: \fB[Section]\fR headers and \fBkey=value\fR
lines.\& Lines starting with \fB#\fR or \fB;\fR are comments.\& Values are taken
verbatim after the first \fB=\fR: there are no inline comments, so a colour like
\fBbase=#1e1e2e\fR needs no quoting.\& Every file may carry \fBFormat=1\fR.\&
.PP
Your own files live in \fI~/.\&config/kome/\fR and override the shipped ones with
the same name: copy a shipped file there to change it.\&
.PP
.SH KOME.CONF
.PP
\fI~/.\&config/kome/kome.\&conf\fR holds global settings.\&
.PP
\fB[General]\fR
.RS 4
\fBPreset=\fR\fIname\fR
.RS 4
The preset used by \fBkome apply\fR, \fBkome deps\fR and \fBkome doctor\fR when
none is given (without it, they use the active one).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBRefreshPanel=on\fR|\fBoff\fR
.RS 4
Whether kome refreshes Plasma'\&s panel after changing icons (default
\fBon\fR).\& With \fBoff\fR, kome only says how to do it.\&
.PP
.RE
.RE
\fB[Units]\fR
.RS 4
\fIunit\fR\fB=on\fR|\fBoff\fR
.RS 4
Turn a unit on or off, overriding its default.\& \fBrendering\fR, \fBpanel\fR
and \fBwallpaper\fR are off unless turned on here.\&
.PP
.RE
.RE
Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[General]
Preset=mocha

[Units]
rendering=on
wallpaper=on
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH PRESETS
.PP
\fIpresets/<name>.\&ini\fR describes one look.\& The file name is the preset'\&s name.\&
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[Preset]
name=Catppuccin Mocha
palette=catppuccin-mocha
style=soft
mode=dark
icon_theme=Papirus-Dark
icon_accent=violet
cursor_theme=catppuccin-mocha-lavender-cursors
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBname\fR
.RS 4
Full name, shown by \fBkome list\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpalette\fR, \fBstyle\fR
.RS 4
The palette and style files to use (required).\& Mixing the palette of one
look with the style of another is allowed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmode\fR
.RS 4
\fBdark\fR or \fBlight\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBicon_theme\fR, \fBicon_accent\fR
.RS 4
The icon theme, and an optional folder colour of that theme (for Papirus:
\fBblue\fR, \fBviolet\fR, \fBindigo\fR, \fBteal\fR…).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBcursor_theme\fR
.RS 4
The cursor theme (optional: if it is not installed, the cursor is left as
is).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBcolor_scheme\fR
.RS 4
Use this installed KDE colour scheme instead of generating one from the
palette (e.\&g.\& \fBBreezeDark\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwallpaper\fR
.RS 4
An image, as an absolute path or starting with \fI~/\fR (used only when the
\fBwallpaper\fR unit is on).\&
.PP
.RE
Any palette or style key may also appear here, and wins: e.\&g.\&
\fBaccent=#cba6f7\fR.\&
.PP
.SH PALETTES
.PP
\fIpalettes/<name>.\&ini\fR has a \fB[Palette]\fR section with all 27 colour roles, as
\fB#rrggbb\fR:
.PP
\fBbase mantle crust surface0 surface1 surface2 overlay0 overlay1 overlay2 text
subtext0 subtext1 rosewater flamingo pink mauve red maroon peach yellow green
teal sky sapphire blue lavender accent\fR
.PP
A palette missing a role, or with a value that is not a colour, is an error.\&
.PP
.SH STYLES
.PP
\fIstyles/<name>.\&ini\fR has a \fB[Style]\fR section:
.PP
\fBfont_ui\fR, \fBfont_mono\fR
.RS 4
The interface and monospace fonts.\& Empty means KDE'\&s own default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfont_size\fR
.RS 4
Size in points, a whole number (default 10).\& Small fonts are 2 points
less.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdecoration\fR
.RS 4
\fBklassy\fR or \fBbreeze\fR (empty: leave the windows alone).\& Klassy is
optional: if it is not installed, windows keep their frame.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwindow_radius\fR
.RS 4
Window corner radius in pixels (Klassy).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwindow_buttons\fR
.RS 4
\fBcircles\fR (small circles in the accent colour, their symbols always shown
in a softer tone of the same colour; the colours come from
\fItemplates/decoration/button-colors.\&in\fR) or \fBicons\fR (Klassy).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBbuttons_left\fR, \fBbuttons_right\fR
.RS 4
Title bar buttons in KWin'\&s letters: \fBM\fR menu, \fBS\fR all desktops, \fBH\fR
help, \fBI\fR minimise, \fBA\fR maximise, \fBX\fR close (empty: KDE'\&s default).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBplasma_style\fR
.RS 4
The look of Plasma'\&s panel, widgets and notifications: \fBklassy\fR
(Klassy'\&s, dark or light to match the mode; optional), \fBbreeze\fR (KDE'\&s
default), or the id of any installed Plasma style.\& Empty: leave it alone.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwidget_style\fR
.RS 4
The widget style inside apps: \fBklassy\fR (optional) or \fBbreeze\fR.\& Empty:
leave it alone.\& Apps started after the change use it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBblur\fR
.RS 4
\fBon\fR or \fBoff\fR: KWin'\&s blur behind translucent panels and menus.\& Empty:
leave it alone.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBanimation_speed\fR
.RS 4
\fBnormal\fR, \fBfast\fR, \fBslow\fR or \fBinstant\fR (no animations).\& Empty: leave it
alone.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpanel\fR
.RS 4
The panel layout, used only when the \fBpanel\fR unit is on: \fBbar\fR (Plasma'\&s
default bar), \fBdock\fR (a floating dock centred at the bottom) or \fBtopbar\fR
(a thin top bar and a dock).\& Every panel is replaced, widgets included;
\fBkome restore\fR brings yours back.\& Empty: leave the panels alone.\& Your own
layout can be written as \fItemplates/panel/<name>.\&js\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH TEMPLATES
.PP
Each unit fills its templates from these values.\& To change what a unit
writes, copy its template to \fI~/.\&config/kome/templates/<unit>/\fR and edit the
copy.\& Panel layouts are JavaScript for Plasma'\&s scripting instead (see the
shipped \fIbar.\&js\fR).\& In templates, \fB{{role}}\fR is a value, \fB{{role:rgb}}\fR a colour as
\fBr,g,b\fR, and \fBmix(a,b,t)\fR, \fBlighten(a,t)\fR, \fBdarken(a,t)\fR and
\fBby_mode(dark,light)\fR derive colours.\&
.PP
.SH KEYS
.PP
Value keys are lowercase \fBsnake_case\fR; section names are CamelCase.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBkome\fR(1)
